{"name":"Innuendo","hex":"#a4b0c4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"innuendo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A derogatory hint or reference to, or (often sexual) insinuation about, a person or thing.","A remark that is suggestive of something sexual without stating it explicitly."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To interpret (something libellous or slanderous) in terms of what was implied."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innuendo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Innuendo","blocks":[{"text":"An innuendo is a hint, insinuation or intimation about a person or thing, especially of a denigrating or derogatory nature. It can also be a remark or question, typically disparaging, that works obliquely by allusion. In the latter sense, the intention is often to insult or accuse someone in such a way that one's words, taken literally, are innocent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Animal_Flyer.jpg/330px-Animal_Flyer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Innuendo","wikidata":"Q1499811"},{"title":"Innuendo (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Innuendo is the fourteenth studio album by the British rock band Queen, released on 4 February 1991 through Parlophone in the United Kingdom and Hollywood Records in the United States."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f7/Queen_Innuendo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Innuendo_(album)","wikidata":"Q210048"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Strechit_ca1800-1810_non-sidesaddle_sailor_caricature.jpg/500px-Strechit_ca1800-1810_non-sidesaddle_sailor_caricature.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Strechit_ca1800-1810_non-sidesaddle_sailor_caricat